 '🌱', 'Sesame seed', 0.5),

(6,
 'Your baby is growing rapidly this week. The embryo is now about the size of a lentil. Major development is happening, including early brain development, spinal cord growth, heart development, and formation of tiny arm and leg buds. In many pregnancies, the heartbeat may begin to be detectable around this stage. Even though your baby is still very tiny, important organs and body systems are developing quickly.',
 'Pregnancy hormones increase significantly during Week 6. Your body is working hard to support placenta development, hormone production, early fetal growth, and increased blood supply. Many women begin feeling stronger pregnancy symptoms during this stage. Fatigue may become more noticeable.',
